{
  "result": "If I could change the world in just one way, I'd make empathy a little bit louder than fear.\n\nNot to erase all our differences or disagreements \u2014 those are part of what makes us human \u2014 but to give everyone the instinct, even just for a moment, to really see the world through someone else's eyes. To feel what it's like to be them.\n\nI think so much of the hurt in the world comes from feeling unseen, unheard, or alone in our struggles. If curiosity about each other came more naturally than judgment or fear, I think a lot of other things would start to heal too \u2014 how we handle conflict, inequality, loneliness, even how we take care of the planet.\n\nJust a little more: *\u201cOh, you\u2019re a whole person with a story, just like me.\u201d*\n\nA small spark, really \u2014 but sparks spread.\n\nWhat about you? What would you change?",
